{"agent":"fleet-capskew","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new filter short-circuits on `not version_key(c.version)`, so any capability whose `version` is absent or unparseable is unconditionally retained in `caps`. That directly contradicts the rule this same change states in its own comment two lines above — \"A capability counts only once a release that ships it has stamped this log\" — because a capability with no version has no release stamp at all, yet is still counted. Concretely: a log written by the 0.2.3 agents plus one capability event that omits `version` (the natural way to \"test a capability without announcing it\" that the intent asks for) takes the first operand — `version_key(None)`/`version_key(\"\")` is falsy, so the whole disjunction is `True` and the entry survives the comprehension untouched. The older clones therefore still see an unstamped, unknown capability announced exactly as they did before the fix, so B27842cfecd's stall is only removed for events that happen to carry a well-formed newer `version`; a blank/missing version reintroduces it. (If `version_key` raises on `None` rather than returning falsy, this line is instead a crash on such an event.) The filter should treat an absent version as \"not stamped\" and drop it, or the comment's stated rule is not what the code implements.","digest":"17e03e39357e48fa","location":"ddflow/core/events.py:411","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/events.py:411"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The fix narrows the capability part of the skew guard to \"the kind being written\" only for the `_patch_skew` branch that is reached with a *non-falsy* kind. `_write` explicitly allows an ungoverned write (`gap = capability_gap(facts.capabilities, kind) if kind else None`), and for such a write the direct conflict check is skipped (treated as \"no direct conflict possible\"), yet `_judge_skew(..., kind=kind)` then forwards the falsy `kind` into `_patch_skew`, whose `kind is None` branch still uses the blanket `capabilities_ahead(facts.capabilities)`:\n\n    gap = (capabilities_ahead(facts.capabilities) if kind is None\n           else capability_gap(facts.capabilities, kind) is not None)\n\nSo for any write whose `kind` is `None`, an unrelated recorded capability event still makes `_patch_skew` return False, the \"patch skew warns instead of refusing\" branch is not taken, and `_judge_skew` raises `SkewRefused` — i.e. exactly the B27842cfecd stall this change is supposed to remove, and exactly the \"merge through the skew guard\" symptom in the bug report (merges/unclassified writes are the natural falsy-kind writers). Concrete input: log contains `ddflow.capabilities` for `evidence-blobs`/0.2.4, running ddflow is 0.2.3, a write is issued with `kind=None` (or any falsy kind). `_write`'s direct check yields no gap, but `_patch_skew(None)` sees `capabilities_ahead` True and the write is refused instead of being allowed under `OLDER_MARK`. Note the asymmetry the same guard introduces: a caller that omits `kind` gets the default `\"\"`, for which `capability_gap(caps, \"\")` is (for an unknown/empty kind) not a gap, so the identical write is allowed; only the explicitly-passed `None` is blanket-refused. Since the stated policy is \"refuse only on a DIRECT conflict (D-compat: older clones preserve what they do not understand)\", `_patch_skew` should apply the same \"no kind ⇒ no capability conflict\" rule that `_write` already applies, or the direct check and this path must agree.","digest":"96c7cb9625be4e4d","location":"ddflow/infra/log.py:_patch_skew (called from _judge_skew)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/infra/log.py:_patch_skew (called from _judge_skew)"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The suite never exercises the rule the fix is actually about — \"the skew guard must refuse only on a DIRECT conflict\". The unstamped case (test 1) is covered, but the only stamped case (test 2) asserts `SkewRefused` for the very kind *named inside the capability* (`kinds=[\"gate.passed\"]` and `log.append(\"gate.passed\", ...)`), so it cannot tell a genuine direct conflict apart from a blanket version-skew refusal. Concretely, an implementation whose guard refuses *every* append once any `ddflow.seen` event records a version newer than the running one — regardless of the kind being written — passes all three tests: test 1 (no `ddflow.seen` written, so the guard is inert) succeeds, test 2 raises as expected, and test 3 only checks the writer side. That implementation still reproduces the reported symptom (a newer-version event in the live log blocking `gate record ... passed`), yet the regression test stays green. A case where the log is stamped by 0.2.4 and the 0.2.3 agent writes an unrelated kind (or a kind the evidence-blobs capability only *extends* additively) is needed to pin \"only a direct conflict refuses\".","digest":"1a5b5d307a27544c","location":"tests/test_capability_event_skew.py:61 (test_a_released_capability_still_refuses_a_direct_conflict)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_capability_event_skew.py:61 (test_a_released_capability_still_refuses_a_direct_conflict)"}],"chunks_total":5,"coverage":"5/5 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":13956,"diff_sha":"89ec952c522fd1f0339546e9bb8c38bd0a368692da197c8561560f31c2dff3a9","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":749.8,"family":"deepseek","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"7876f17d964e7ce0","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B27842cfecd.critic.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261015T192531Z-18f08284.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5],"reviewed_head":"25629f57c5d36f51f61ed69393046018ec3c9bbf","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/core/events.py:411","ddflow/infra/log.py:_patch_skew (called from _judge_skew)","tests/test_capability_event_skew.py:61 (test_a_released_capability_still_refuses_a_direct_conflict)"],"tree_sha":"25629f57c5d3+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"3 finding(s)"},"id":"e36665015160e776b5c012e59","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":64818,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B27842cfecd","ts":"2026-10-15T19:38:01.955837Z"}
